  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule in the supplied records.",
    "No IV-comparator or AUC-based F data for the query itself.",
    "Human absolute F for the closest analog pirfenidone has not been determined (C27).",
    "L5 records are permeability/efflux measurements, not direct intestinal metabolism or systemic F measurements.",
    "First-pass hepatic metabolism and clearance for the query are not directly measured."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Prediction remains high and is strengthened: the query is a small neutral phenyl-substituted pyrazolone with favorable physicochemical properties; the closest analog edaravone shows very high intestinal permeability with no efflux barrier; pirfenidone shows high oral bioavailability and 46% rat F; L3 exposure records show rapid absorption; L4 records show complete intestinal absorption for related drugs; and L5 records provide additional mechanistic support for high permeability and negligible efflux. No affirmative evidence supports F < 20%. Confidence stays moderate because no direct F measurement exists for the query."
